@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki to Provisioning Subscription Integration
	Testing to assure that koroneiki account subscription information transfers properly to the account index.

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I tear down the teams on koroneiki with the following names
	| Koroneiki Partner |
	| Updated Partner   |
	* I tear down the team roles on koroneiki with the following names
	| Partner |
	* I tear down the external links for the product "A Liferay DXP Product" on koroneiki with the following entity id values
	| A Liferay DXP Product |
	* I tear down the external links for the product "A Liferay Portal Product" on koroneiki with the following entity id values
	| A Liferay Portal Product |
	* I tear down the external links for the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following entity id values
	| Platinum Subscription |
	* I tear down the external links for the product "Gold Subscription" on koroneiki with the following entity id values
	| Gold Subscription |
	* I tear down the external links for the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" on koroneiki with the following entity id and domain values
	| ${staticDossieraAccountKey}   | salesforce |
	| ${staticDossieraAccountKey}   | dossiera   |
	| ${staticSalesforceProjectKey} | salesforce |
	* I tear down the product consumptions on koroneiki made by the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" for the following products
	| A Liferay DXP Product    |
	| A Liferay Portal Product |
	| Liferay DXP Production   |
	| Platinum Subscription    |
	| Gold Subscription        |
	* I tear down the product consumptions on koroneiki made by the account "Onepro - ${staticCompanyName}" for the following products
	| A Liferay DXP Product    |
	| A Liferay Portal Product |
	| Liferay DXP Production   |
	| Platinum Subscription    |
	| Gold Subscription        |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" for the following products
	| A Liferay DXP Product    |
	| A Liferay Portal Product |
	| Liferay DXP Production   |
	| Platinum Subscription    |
	| Gold Subscription        |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Onepro - ${staticCompanyName}" for the following products
	| A Liferay DXP Product    |
	| A Liferay Portal Product |
	| Liferay DXP Production   |
	| Platinum Subscription    |
	| Gold Subscription        |
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| A Liferay DXP Product    |
	| A Liferay Portal Product |
	| Platinum Subscription    |
	| Gold Subscription        |
	* I tear down the contact roles on koroneiki with the following names
	| Liferay Account Customer Role |
 	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korpro - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Onepro - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| KORPROKORPRO |
	| ONEPROONEPRO |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Korpro - ${staticCompanyName} |

Scenario: View platinum subscription
	Testing the ability to create a platinum subcription in Dossiera and viewing the subscription in the provisioning account details page 

	Given I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	And I generate a provisioning company name
	And I generate a provisioning project name
	And I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message on sandbox with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRO                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Contact Role                           | Liferay Account Customer Role              |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRO                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | A Liferay DXP Product                      |
	| Project Name                           | Korpro - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I wait for "10" seconds
	And I create a product consumption for an account with the name "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" and the product "A Liferay DXP Product" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1 | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2 | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3 | propertyValue3 |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "kwSgiajslgb7ecsD"
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the product with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name         | A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Provisioned  | 1                     |
	| Purchased    | 1                     |
	| Status       | ACTIVE                |
	And I should be able to view the product with the name "Platinum Subscription" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name         | Platinum Subscription |
	| Provisioned  | 0                     |
	| Purchased    | 1                     |
	| Status       | ACTIVE                |
	When I click on the "Inactive" product tab
	Then I should not be able to view the product with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" on the account details page
	And I should not be able to view the product with the name "Platinum Subscription" on the account details page
	When I click on the "All" product tab
	Then I should be able to view the product with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name         | A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Provisioned  | 1                     |
	| Purchased    | 1                     |
	| Status       | ACTIVE                |
	And I should be able to view the product with the name "Platinum Subscription" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name         | Platinum Subscription |
	| Provisioned  | 0                     |
	| Purchased    | 1                     |
	| Status       | ACTIVE                |
	When I click on the "A Liferay DXP Product" subscription link
	Then I should be able to view the following subscription values in the subscription details page
	| Name   | A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Status | ACTIVE                |
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Platinum Subscription" subscription link
	Then I should be able to view the following subscription values in the subscription details page
	| Name   | Platinum Subscription |
	| Status | ACTIVE                |
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" on the provisioning index
	When I click on the "History" tab
	And I generate the account ID value for "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}"
	Then the history entry in position number "9" with the field value "quantity" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Product Purchase > A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Update Field Name           | quantity                                              |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                   |
	| Update Field New Value      | 1                                                     |
	And the history entry in position number "9" with the field value "accountId" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Product Purchase > A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Update Field Name           | accountId                                             |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                   |
	| Update Field New Value      | ${staticAccountId}                                    |
	And the history entry in position number "9" with the field value "status" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Product Purchase > A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Update Field Name           | status                                                |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                   |
	| Update Field New Value      | 0                                                     |
	And the history entry in position number "9" with the field value "sizing" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Product Purchase > A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Update Field Name           | sizing                                                |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                   |
	| Update Field New Value      | Sizing 1                                              |
	And the history entry in position number "9" with the field value "environment" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Product Purchase > A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Update Field Name           | environment                                           |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                   |
	| Update Field New Value      | Production                                            |
	And the history entry in position number "9" with the field value "productType" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Product Purchase > A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Update Field Name           | productType                                           |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                   |
	| Update Field New Value      | New                                                   |
	Then the history entry in position number "10" with the field value "quantity" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Product Purchase > Platinum Subscription |
	| Update Field Name           | quantity                                              |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                   |
	| Update Field New Value      | 1                                                     |
	And the history entry in position number "10" with the field value "accountId" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Product Purchase > Platinum Subscription |
	| Update Field Name           | accountId                                             |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                   |
	| Update Field New Value      | ${staticAccountId}                                    |
	And the history entry in position number "10" with the field value "status" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Product Purchase > Platinum Subscription |
	| Update Field Name           | status                                                |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                   |
	| Update Field New Value      | 0                                                     |
	And the history entry in position number "10" with the field value "productType" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Product Purchase > Platinum Subscription |
	| Update Field Name           | productType                                           |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                   |
	| Update Field New Value      | New                                                   |
	And the history entry in position number "11" with the field value "additionalProp1" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Koroneiki Admin > Added Product Consumption > A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Update Field Name           | additionalProp1                                                     |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                                 |
	| Update Field New Value      | propertyValue1                                                      |
	And the history entry in position number "11" with the field value "additionalProp2" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Koroneiki Admin > Added Product Consumption > A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Update Field Name           | additionalProp2                                                     |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                                 |
	| Update Field New Value      | propertyValue2                                                      |
	And the history entry in position number "11" with the field value "additionalProp3" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Koroneiki Admin > Added Product Consumption > A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Update Field Name           | additionalProp3                                                     |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                                 |
	| Update Field New Value      | propertyValue3                                                      |

Scenario: View non perpetual subscription
	Testing the ability to create a platinum subcription in Dossiera and updating the subscription to be non perpetual before viewing the subscription in the provisioning account details page 

	Given I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	And I generate a provisioning company name
	And I generate a provisioning project name
	And I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message on sandbox with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRO                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Contact Role                           | Liferay Account Customer Role              |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRO                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | A Liferay DXP Product                      |
	| Project Name                           | Korpro - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I wait for "10" seconds
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I generate static full start and end dates
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" for the product "A Liferay DXP Product" to have the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" for the product "Platinum Subscription" to have the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product consumption for an account with the name "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" and the product "A Liferay DXP Product" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Product Purchase        | true            |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1 | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2 | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3 | propertyValue3 |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "kwSgiajslgb7ecsD"
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the product with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name             | A Liferay DXP Product                         |
	| Support Life     | ${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullEndDate} |
	| Next Term Starts | false                                         |
	| Provisioned      | 1                                             |
	| Purchased        | 1                                             |
	| Status           | ACTIVE                                        |
	And I should be able to view the product with the name "Platinum Subscription" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name             | Platinum Subscription                         |
	| Support Life     | ${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullEndDate} |
	| Next Term Starts | false                                         |
	| Provisioned      | 0                                             |
	| Purchased        | 1                                             |
	| Status           | ACTIVE                                        |
	When I click on the "Inactive" product tab
	Then I should not be able to view the product with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" on the account details page
	Then I should not be able to view the product with the name "Platinum Subscription" on the account details page
	When I click on the "All" product tab
	Then I should be able to view the product with the name "A Liferay DXP Product" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name             | A Liferay DXP Product                         |
	| Support Life     | ${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullEndDate} |
	| Next Term Starts | false                                         |
	| Provisioned      | 1                                             |
	| Purchased        | 1                                             |
	| Status           | ACTIVE                                        |
	And I should be able to view the product with the name "Platinum Subscription" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name             | Platinum Subscription                         |
	| Support Life     | ${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullEndDate} |
	| Next Term Starts | false                                         |
	| Provisioned      | 0                                             |
	| Purchased        | 1                                             |
	| Status           | ACTIVE                                        |
	When I click on the "A Liferay DXP Product" subscription link
	Then I should be able to view the following subscription values in the subscription details page
	| Name         | A Liferay DXP Product                               |
	| Status       | ACTIVE                                              |
	| Support Life | ${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullEndDate}       |
	| Grace Period | ${staticFullOriginalEndDate} - ${staticFullEndDate} |
	And I should be able to view the term with the start date to end date "${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullEndDate}" and the following values
	| Start - End Date           | ${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullEndDate}       |
	| Grace Period               | ${staticFullOriginalEndDate} - ${staticFullEndDate} |
	| Provisioned                | 1                                                   |
	| Purchased                  | 1                                                   |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}                   |
	| Status                     | APPROVED                                            |
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Platinum Subscription" subscription link
	Then I should be able to view the following subscription values in the subscription details page
	| Name         | Platinum Subscription                               |
	| Status       | ACTIVE                                              |
	| Support Life | ${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullEndDate}       |
	| Grace Period | ${staticFullOriginalEndDate} - ${staticFullEndDate} |
	And I should be able to view the term with the start date to end date "${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullEndDate}" and the following values
	| Start - End Date           | ${staticFullStartDate} - ${staticFullEndDate}       |
	| Grace Period               | ${staticFullOriginalEndDate} - ${staticFullEndDate} |
	| Provisioned                | 0                                                   |
	| Purchased                  | 1                                                   |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}                   |
	| Status                     | APPROVED                                            |
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" on the provisioning index
	When I click on the "History" tab
	And I generate the account ID value for "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}"
	Then the history entry in position number "9" with the field value "quantity" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Product Purchase > A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Update Field Name           | quantity                                              |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                   |
	| Update Field New Value      | 1                                                     |
	And the history entry in position number "9" with the field value "accountId" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Product Purchase > A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Update Field Name           | accountId                                             |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                   |
	| Update Field New Value      | ${staticAccountId}                                    |
	And the history entry in position number "9" with the field value "status" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Product Purchase > A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Update Field Name           | status                                                |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                   |
	| Update Field New Value      | 0                                                     |
	And the history entry in position number "9" with the field value "sizing" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Product Purchase > A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Update Field Name           | sizing                                                |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                   |
	| Update Field New Value      | Sizing 1                                              |
	And the history entry in position number "9" with the field value "environment" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Product Purchase > A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Update Field Name           | environment                                           |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                   |
	| Update Field New Value      | Production                                            |
	And the history entry in position number "9" with the field value "productType" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Product Purchase > A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Update Field Name           | productType                                           |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                   |
	| Update Field New Value      | New                                                   |
	Then the history entry in position number "10" with the field value "quantity" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Product Purchase > Platinum Subscription |
	| Update Field Name           | quantity                                              |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                   |
	| Update Field New Value      | 1                                                     |
	And the history entry in position number "10" with the field value "accountId" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
